KZ2 patch 2098: hide the mouse pointer over the focused game window (WM_SETCURSOR), show it again on focus loss.

A tester's hand play (2026-10-22) and every frame of its screen recordings showed the Windows arrow over the game: nothing
hid it (the window class sets IDC_ARROW). WM_SETCURSOR with an HTCLIENT hit on the focused game window now sets no
cursor, in windowed, borderless and fullscreen alike; over the title bar or borders and while another window has the
focus, DefWindowProc shows the arrow. WM_ACTIVATE applies the new state at once (WM_SETCURSOR only comes with mouse
movement); WM_KILLFOCUS puts the arrow back. RSX_CURSOR=1 keeps the arrow. The decision is a pure function in
rsx_cursor.h (host test tools/runtime/test_cursor.sh). No ClipCursor and no raw input: mouse look is not wired
(keyboard and mouse is backlog). KZ2_TEST_DISPLAY gets two steps for tests: `mouse` (pointer to the client
centre) and `cursor` (logs GetCursor(): HIDDEN or SHOWN, focus, pointer over the client area). Under Xwayland (a Wine session on a Wayland desktop) whether a hidden Wine cursor reaches the
Wayland pointer is not verified (the patch's own test checked it under Xvfb only).
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_cursor.h
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+/* KZ2 patch 2098: the mouse cursor over the game window (pure decision, host test tools/runtime/test_cursor.c).
+ * The pointer is hidden while it is over the client area of the focused game window, in every display mode
+ * (windowed, borderless, fullscreen); over the title bar or the borders, or when another window has the focus, the
+ * normal arrow shows. RSX_CURSOR=1 keeps the arrow everywhere. No ClipCursor or raw input: mouse look is not wired. */
+#ifndef RSX_CURSOR_H
+#define RSX_CURSOR_H
+
+/* hit_client: the WM_SETCURSOR hit test is HTCLIENT; focused: the game window is the foreground window;
+ * keep_arrow: RSX_CURSOR=1. -> 1 = hide the pointer (SetCursor(NULL)), 0 = leave it to DefWindowProc. */
+static inline int rsx_cursor_hidden(int hit_client, int focused, int keep_arrow)
+{
+    return hit_client && focused && !keep_arrow;
+}
+
+#endif

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

